  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "Midnight systems",
    "overview": "This records the incumbent portfolio identity named in the global stylesheet: blue-black surfaces, periwinkle accents, restrained borders, and clear technical typography. The user explicitly confirmed preserving the dark blue identity. This is a scan of implemented work, with no new visual world or approved system replacement.\n\nThe blog extends that identity with a wide, compact article index and a full-size editable article. The user's Dan Luu reference guides the blog toward plain linked writing with minimal clutter. Compact author controls sit above the shared reading and editing document layout. Optional interactive figures sit within that reading flow; their plain-text configuration stays editable by people and agents. This is a surface-specific refinement; the homepage retains its incumbent visual system.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Blue-black surfaces with restrained periwinkle emphasis.",
      "Inter reading text and JetBrains Mono for code and technical identity.",
      "Fine dividers, tonal panels, and gently rounded controls."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Shared Identity Rule",
        "body": "Extend the existing dark blue palette rather than introducing a replacement identity for a new surface.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Visible Interaction Rule",
        "body": "Blog keyboard focus uses a visible accent outline; selection uses dark text on the accent fill. Preserve both when adding controls.",
        "section": "components"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** reuse the incumbent dark blue palette and font families.",
